is the amount the next collect call or checkout session charges. To total everything overdue, add the outstanding_money of the entries whose status is overdue. Always 0 unless the invoice is open or partially_paid. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. object.customer (Optional): {@see ExpandedCustomerSummaryInput} or null. Summary of the billed customer. Returned only with expand=customer. Present only when `expand` includes `customer`; `null` when expanded and there is no related customer. object.customer.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see ExpandedCustomerSummaryInput}. A customer's summary fields, returned in place of a customer ID when the customer is expanded. object.customer.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.customer_id (Optional): string. Customer billed by this invoice. Absent when the invoice has no customer. Example: "cus_01KEZF7C006X9JK6NZNA2SM9XD". object.delivery_mode (Optional): string. How issue delivered the invoice. Value enum: "email", "caller_managed". object.due_date (Optional): string. Calendar due date in YYYY-MM-DD format, interpreted in timezone (UTC when absent). The outstanding balance becomes overdue only after this date ends. Automatic collection runs at the later of issue and the start of this date. With payment terms, issue computes this date from issued_at. Absent when there is no due date. Format: date. Example: "2026-08-02". object.external_reference_id (Required): string or null. Caller-owned identifier for this resource in an external system. Use it as your sync key: it isn't printed on the invoice. `null` when unset. minLength: 1. maxLength: 255. Example: "warehouse-1842". object.footer (Required): string or null. Fine print at the bottom of the invoice and PDF. It cannot change after issue. `null` when unset. object.invoice_id (Required): string. Flint invoice ID. Example: "inv_01KEZF7C00A5GEBMWHEAJFSAR4". object.invoice_number (Optional): string. Sequential document number assigned when the invoice