e1 and city, and US ones always have state and postal_code. Delivery quote destinations, buyer locations and postal-code tax locations hold only what was provided, such as postal_code and country. object.schedule_entries (Required): Array of {@see InvoiceScheduleEntryInput}. The payment schedule, in schedule order. Always [] when the invoice has no schedule and is collected in one balance. object.schedule_entries[] (Value): {@see InvoiceScheduleEntryInput}. One payment on an invoice's payment schedule, such as a deposit, installment, or balance, with its due time, amounts, and status. object.scheduled_issue_at (Required): string or null. When Flint will issue and deliver this draft. `null` when no issue is scheduled. Cleared when the draft is issued or voided, or when you send null. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.service_date (Required): string or null. The calendar date of the billed service, in YYYY-MM-DD format. The invoice and PDF print it as written, without timezone conversion. `null` when unset. Format: date. Example: "2026-08-02". object.snapshot (Optional): {@see InvoiceSnapshotInput}. The billing content of the invoice: line items, discounts, charges, tip, and tax. A draft previews the backing order; issue freezes it, and later order changes don't reach an issued invoice. A frozen copy of an issued invoice's content, including line items, charges, discounts, tax identities, and pricing amounts. object.status (Required): string. Current invoice status. paid and credited close the current balance and can reopen to open or partially_paid after a payment or credit allocation reversal; invoice.reopened reports that change. An uncollectible invoice accepts manual recovery payments and becomes paid when fully recovered; reversals restore the write-off. voided is final. Refunds change refund_status without reopening the balance. A lost dispute leaves paid_money, the balance, and status unchanged; collecting it again requires a new invoice. Value enum: "draft", "open", "partially_paid", "paid", "voided", "uncollectible", "credited". object.subscription_id (Required): string or null. The subscription the backing order belongs to, copied when the draft is created and never changed. `null` when the order isn't part of a subscription. Example: "sub_01KEZF7C00BVRE8YDBXQB74BBM". object.supported_actions (Required): Array of string. Lifecycle actions Flint accepts for this resource now, based on stored state. Independent of the caller's permissions; each action still requires its route's scope. Always [] when no action is available. [] enum: "collect", "issue", "mark_uncollectible", "void". object.supported_actions[] (Value): string.  Value enum: "collect", "issue", "mark_uncollectible", "void". object.timezone (Optional): string. IANA time zone snapshot for invoice due dates, reminders, and late fee calendar days. Taken from the merchant's timezone when the draft is written, or UTC when unset. Later merchant changes do not alter this invoice's calendar. object.uncollectible_at (Optional): string. When the invoice was marked uncollectible. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.updated_at (Required): string. When the invoice last changed. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.version (Required): integer. Current invoice version. Send this as expected_version when updating the draft. Format: int64. minimum: 1. object.viewed_at (Optional): string. When the buyer first opened the invoice through its hosted invoice link. Recorded on a best-effort basis. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.voided_at (Optional): string. When the invoice was voided. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.written_off_money (Required): {@see MoneyValueInput}. The balance written off when the invoice was marked uncollectible, including unpaid late fees. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. previous_attri